            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Happyschmoopies"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Can't believe how easy it is to freshen up a bottle of store bought dressing. I think the key is to start with a good base - I used family style italian from that handsome blue-eyed actor. The sugar took the edge off the acidic tartness you can get from the vinegar. The fresh garlic brightened up the flavor. If I am in a pinch and don't have time to make a homeade dressing - this will do the trick.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-23T14:46:21.550Z"
